                ],
                "notes": "This game features use of unrealistic alien weapons and animated violence in a fictional storyline played out by comic themed characters."
            },
            "ratings": null,
            "reviews": {
                "query_summary": {
                    "num_reviews": 1,
                    "review_score": 0,
                    "review_score_desc": "8 user reviews",
                    "total_positive": 6,
                    "total_negative": 2,
                    "total_reviews": 8
                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "55704459",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197981111953",
                            "num_reviews": 380,
                            "playtime_forever": 236,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 150,
                            "last_played": 1571845373
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Alienautics is a good third-person-shooter in early-access. It tells an interesting sci-fi story in form of ingame cinematics. The handling is good, the shooting nice and impactful, but a bit difficult to learn, platform jumping is a bit slippery. The game is in general not an easy one, the enemies are hard and mastering all the cover-mechanics and the shield is a must to stay alive, this gives the game a strategic touch. But if you die, a checkpoint is always near, so it is no real pain. The music and the sound effects are good. The graphics are very nice and clean, but a bit outdated. Sadly the game uses a third-party launcher, which produce no problems, but i would prefer a game without this kind of software. For an early-access title it is in a good state, the first part is fully playable, i found no major bugs.  Check my gameplay video to see, if this is a game for you.\n\nGameplay video:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GD00W6YXun0",
                        "timestamp_created": 1571673359,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1571673592,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 12,
                        "votes_funny": 3,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6263554692268372,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": false,
                        "received_for_free": true,
                        "written_during_early_access": true,
                        "developer_response": "Thank you so much for taking the time to review the game. I'm glad to know you enjoyed the experience. \n\nI wanted to clarify the user registration requirement. The game uses an official account to keep the game data unified from other game platforms. Alienautics will be available on a few other digital game stores on full release. Keeping a user account helps to manage the player base more efficiently. It works very well for indie studios because we don't have a big PR and marketing department to keep in touch with the player base from different platforms. \n\nThank you so much for playing Alienautics. Your feedback has been very helpful.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1571722052,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
                ],
